# Round 144 — the evolution-algebra problem; two counterexample searches (timed out); conjecture finders

* 2610.22248, open problem l. 1351–1354 ("for every finite connected graph G, A(G) ≅ A_RW(G) iff G is regular or
  biregular"; A(G): e_i² = Σ_(j∼i) e_j; A_RW(G): e_i² = Σ_(j∼i) e_j / deg(i); ARBITRARY field 𝕜). Known by the authors
  for non-singular graphs. Natural-basis scalings force c_j = c_i²/deg(i) for j ∼ i, hence equal neighbour degrees and
  c_i³ = deg(i)² deg(j): regular or biregular, over 𝕜 containing the needed cube roots. Over Q the scaling system
  has no solution for P3 (c³ = 4), K_(1,3) (c³ = 9) and K_(2,3) (c³ = 18). Caveat: uniqueness of natural bases
  (Elduque–Labra) needs PERFECT algebras; every non-regular biregular graph has a singular adjacency matrix, so
  other isomorphisms (mixing twin vertices) must be excluded before P3 is a counterexample over Q. Over C: all 143
  connected graphs with ≤ 6 vertices satisfy "scaling solvable ⇔ regular or biregular".
* Factorial separation (2610.25661) and Krzyż-type (2610.23817) searches: timed out; rescoped.
